 Messages exist in English (`en`) and Korean (`ko`), in
 `src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+
+## Keys and roles
+
+Requests carry `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in the data as
+`apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`.
+
+- `viewer`: may only read (GET).
+- `cook`: may also cook recipes (`POST /recipes/:id/cook`), record waste
+  (`POST /batches/:id/waste`), log temperatures (`POST /temperatures`) and
+  enter stock-take counts (`POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`).
+- `manager`: may do everything.
+
+No key or an unknown key is 401 (`unauthorized`); a known key without
+permission is 403 (`forbidden`). Both use the error shape above.
+
+## Audit log
+
+Every authenticated request that changes data (not GET) appends
+`{ at, name, method, path, status }` to `audit` in the data, whatever its
+outcome. `GET /audit` lists them newest first and is for managers only.
